# Keep the build context small and correct. Without this, `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile drags the host node_modules (built for the host OS/arch, not the
# Alpine builder) over the `npm ci` result and copies the stale local build —
# a cross-arch/staleness hazard and a >750 MB context.
#
# .env is NOT committed — it is each developer's local file and can hold
# PLATFORM_BEARER_TOKEN / a dev token — so it never enters the build context.
# Build-time NEXT_PUBLIC_* flags come from Dockerfile ARGs (secure defaults);
# runtime secrets are injected at `docker run` / compose time.

node_modules/
.next/
.git/
.gitignore

# Local env files (may hold secrets). The example stays: it documents the keys.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs and misc
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
